From e3cda4891950ffcfc6e81f6f3856eba62b09fd13 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kob <kob@invalid>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 00:31:45 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 10/13] Playback joins a background flight once its request is
 sent

A Stream fetch never joined a Warm, Queue or Health flight of the same article,
so a background cache-ahead leading the player made it fetch every shared
article twice. Playback now joins a background flight whose request reached a
provider, and replaces it only while the request is still queued.

The hand-off is atomic: Wait gets a send/withdraw state, the pool marks a
request sent just before writing it (a withdrawn one is dropped unrecorded, as
when no slot comes in time), and the cache replaces a background flight only if
it withdraws that request first. The replaced flight is handed the playback
flight and waits for it rather than fetching again. Every traced flight gets a
leader wait for this.

A Warm reader's window is also capped at its own prefetch, so a plain reader on
the Warm workload keeps its read-ahead; warming readers are unchanged.
